    <main>
    

	<h1>Time Zones</h1>

	<p>The Time Zone Database (often called <tt>tz</tt> or <tt>zoneinfo</tt>) contains code and data that represent the
        history of local time for many representative locations worldwide. It is updated periodically to reflect
        changes made by political bodies to time zone boundaries, UTC offsets, and daylight-saving rules.</p>

	<p>The database is primarily intended for software implementers. Its data is expressed as
        machine-readable rules that, together with the reference implementation, allow software to
        automatically calculate local time with the correct UTC offset for any given location. End
        users typically receive updates to this data through their software and operating system
        vendors.</p>

	<h2>Latest version</h2>

	<a class="tile tile-link" href="/time-zones/releases/2026e">
		<img class="tile-link-icon" src="/static/icons/database-clock.svg" alt="">
		<div class="tile-link-content">
			<h2>2026e</h2>
			<div class="tz-released">Released <time class="relative-time" datetime="2026-09-29">2026-09-29</time></div>
			
			<ul class="tz-summary">
				
				<li>Manitoba moves to permanent -05 on 2026-10-31.</li>
				
			</ul>
			
		</div>
		<img class="tile-link-arrow" src="/static/icons/chevron-right.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
	</a>

